{"name":"Pompadour","hex":"#6a1f44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pompadour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A women's hairstyle in which the hair is swept upwards from the face and worn high over the forehead.","A men's hairstyle of the 1950s."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To style hair into a pompadour"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pompadour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Madame de Pompadour","blocks":[{"text":"Jeanne Antoinette Poisson, Marquise de Pompadour, commonly known as Madame de Pompadour, was a member of the French court. She was the official chief mistress of King Louis XV from 1745 to 1751, and remained influential as court favourite until her death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Charles_Andr%C3%A9_Van_Loo_-_Madame_de_Pompadour_en_belle_jardini%C3%A8re_-_v.1754-1755FXD.jpg/330px-Charles_Andr%C3%A9_Van_Loo_-_Madame_de_Pompadour_en_belle_jardini%C3%A8re_-_v.1754-1755FXD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madame_de_Pompadour","wikidata":"Q188965"},{"title":"Pompadour (hairstyle)","blocks":[{"text":"The pompadour is a hairstyle named after Madame de Pompadour (1721–1764), a mistress of King Louis XV of France. There are numerous variations of the style for men, women, and children. The basic concept is having a large volume of hair swept upwards from the face and worn high over the forehead, and sometimes upswept around the sides and back as well."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pompadour_%28PSF%29.png/330px-Pompadour_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pompadour_(hairstyle)","wikidata":"Q14776796"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Boucher%2C_Fran%C3%A7ois_-_Marquise_de_Pompadour_at_the_Toilet-Table.jpg/500px-Boucher%2C_Fra